    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A union of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> formed in 1526 and held together by the Habsburg dynasty, army and Catholic Church.</li><li>It stopped Ottoman expansion at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> in 1529 and 1683 and reconquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a> by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> in 1699.</li><li><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maria-theresa">Maria Theresa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joseph-ii-holy-roman-emperor">Joseph II</a> made it a model of enlightened absolutism before it became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a> in 1804.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The thaler, struck from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jachymov">Joachimsthal</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, gave its name to the dollar.</p></aside>
    </section>

